    "public_url": "hackathons/neurohack-2027-iit-madras-1781449",
    "title": "Neurohack 2027",
    "organization_id": 606,
    "type": "hackathons",
    "subtype": "online_coding_challenge",
    "regn_open": 1,
    "updated_at": "2026-10-28T09:44:51+05:30",
    "region": "hybrid",
    "visibility": "public",
    "details": "<p><strong>Overview</strong></p>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Neurohack is a two-round computational neuroscience hackathon hosted under BIOGEN at SHAASTRA 2026, IIT Madras. Participants will work with real EEG datasets to build pipelines that classify human emotions from brainwave signals, combining signal processing, machine learning, and neuroscience in one challenge.</span></p>\n<p><strong>Eligibility</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Open to undergraduate and postgraduate students.</span></li>\n<li style=\"font-weight: 400;\" aria-level=\"1\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Teams of 1&ndash;4 members.</span></li>\n<li style=\"font-weight: 400;\" aria-level=\"1\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Participants may be from any discipline and any institute; no prior EEG experience is required, but working knowledge of Python is expected.</span></li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Target Audience</strong></p>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Students interested in:</span></p>\n<ul>\n<li style=\"font-weight: 400;\" aria-level=\"1\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Biotechnology &amp; biomedical engineering</span></li>\n<li style=\"font-weight: 400;\" aria-level=\"1\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Neuroscience and cognitive science</span></li>\n<li style=\"font-weight: 400;\" aria-level=\"1\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Computer science, data science and machine learning</span></li>\n<li style=\"font-weight: 400;\" aria-level=\"1\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Signal processing and electronics</span></li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Competition Rounds</strong></p>\n<p><strong>Round 1: Online Quiz</strong></p>\n<p>An online quiz covering basic neuroscience, EEG principles, brain-wave patterns, and Python for data analysis. Top-scoring teams advance to Round 2.</p>\n<p><strong>Round 2: 24-Hour Offline Hackathon</strong></p>\n<p>Selected teams are invited to IIT Madras during SHAASTRA 2026 for a <strong>24-hour hackathon</strong>. Participants receive a preprocessed subset of a public EEG emotion dataset and build a complete pipeline to classify human emotions using signal processing and machine learning.</p>\n<p><strong>Finals at IIT Madras: PPT Presentation</strong></p>\n<p>Each team presents its problem approach, features, model, results, and insights from the brain signals to a panel of judges, followed by a Q&amp;A session.</p>",
